Building
========

This package uses the meson build system.

    meson setup build
    meson compile -C build

Installing
==========

    meson install -C build

This installs, matching the old autotools layout:

- binaries: cbt-util, tap-ctl, lvm-util, td-util, td-rated to sbindir;
  vhd-util, vhd-index, qemu-img, cpumond, tapback to bindir; tapdisk to
  libexecdir
- libraries: libblktapctl, libvhd, libqcow2, libblockcrypto to libdir
- headers: include/{vhd.h,libvhd*.h,vhd-util.h,list.h} to
  includedir/vhd, and the blktap headers to includedir/blktap
- doc files (README, README.md, LICENSE, CONTRIB, MAINTAINERS) to
  datadir/doc/tapdisk
- drivers/blktap to sysconfdir/logrotate.d, drivers/tapdisk-logs.xml
  and drivers/tapdisk-logs/description.xml to
  sysconfdir/xensource/bugtool, drivers/prune_tapdisk_logs to
  sysconfdir/cron.daily
- cpumond.service and tapback.service to the systemd unit directory
  (auto-detected via pkg-config's systemd.pc when available, otherwise
  /usr/lib/systemd/system)

Use the standard meson/autotools-style directory options to relocate
any of this, e.g.:

    meson setup build --prefix=/usr --sysconfdir=/etc

or install into a staging area without touching the running system:

    DESTDIR=/tmp/staging meson install -C build

Running the unit tests
=======================

The mockatests unit tests (cmocka-based) are built by passing -Dtests=true,
and run via `meson test`:

    meson setup build -Dtests=true
    meson compile -C build
    meson test -C build

Coverage (equivalent of the old "make check GCOV=true")
=========================================================

Configure with both the project's GCOV option (which also implies
-Dtests=true) and meson's built-in b_coverage option (which instruments
the production libraries, not just the test binaries):

    meson setup build -DGCOV=true -Db_coverage=true
    meson compile -C build

Then build the lcov/genhtml report and collect the test logs and raw gcov
files with:

    ./collect-test-results.sh build <output-directory>

The HTML report is written to <output-directory>/coverage-html/index.html.
